    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass with 0 failures/errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure requirement for membership level 4 in `Owner.getMembershipLevel()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`).\n\n**The change:** The three creation-time factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for no namesakes) are still capped at 3. Level 4 is now granted only when the owner's **tenure \u2014 whole days from `registrationDate` to today \u2014 exceeds 365**:\n\n```java\nlevel = Math.min(level, 3);\nboolean longTenure = this.registrationDate != null\n    && java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(this.registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365;\nif (longTenure) {\n    level++;\n}\nreturn level;\n```\n\n**Why a new owner never exceeds level 3:** a newly created owner registers today, so its tenure is 0 days (not > 365), and the tenure step never fires. A new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` 0, and a 3-member household maxes the pre-tenure factors at 3 and stays there \u2014 exactly as `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` asserts.\n\nI also updated the method's Javadoc to describe the 1\u20134 range and the tenure rule, and mirrored the existing `getAgeBand()` pattern by null-guarding `registrationDate`.",
